
Project Assignment: Local Network File-Sharing App


1. Objective

Build a Python web application using Flask that allows devices on the same local Wi-Fi/LAN network to upload and download files through a web browser.

2. Prerequisites

Before starting, ensure you have:
• Python 3.8+ installed on your machine.
• Flask installed via terminal/command prompt:bash
pip install flask
Use code with caution.

3. Required Directory Structure

Create the exact folder and file hierarchy below. File and folder names are case-sensitive and must match verbatim:
text
file_share_app/
├── app.py
├── shared_files/
└── templates/
    └── index.html
Use code with caution.

4. Functional Requirements


A. Backend (app.py)

Your Python script must implement the following behaviors in order:
1. Initialization: Import os and required Flask utilities (Flask, request, send_from_directory, render_template). Initialize the Flask app instance (app = Flask(__name__)).
2. Storage Configuration: Define a constant pointing to the 'shared_files' folder. Programmatically ensure this directory exists upon startup (os.makedirs(..., exist_ok=True)).
3. Home & Upload Endpoint (/):
	• Must accept both GET and POST HTTP methods.
	• On POST: Retrieve the uploaded file object from request.files under the key 'file'. Validate that a file was selected and has a non-empty filename, then save it into shared_files/.
	• On GET and POST: Read the current list of filenames inside shared_files/ and render templates/index.html, passing the file list as a template variable named files.
4. Download Endpoint (/download/<filename>):
	• Accept a dynamic <filename> URL parameter.
	• Return the requested file from shared_files/ as a downloadable attachment (as_attachment=True).
5. Server Execution:
	• Inside an if __name__ == '__main__': guard, start the server bound to host '0.0.0.0' and port 5000.

B. Frontend (templates/index.html)

Your HTML template must contain two functional sections:
1. Upload Form:
	• A <form> element using method="post" and enctype="multipart/form-data".
	• One file input (<input type="file" name="file" required>).
	• One submit button (<input type="submit" value="Upload">).
2. File Directory List:
	• A Jinja2 {% for file in files %} loop that generates a list item (<li>) for every filename passed from app.py.
	• Each item must contain an anchor tag (<a href="/download/{{ file }}">{{ file }}</a>) pointing to the download endpoint.

5. Acceptance Criteria (How to Verify It Works)

Your submission is considered complete when all 5 checks pass:
1. Running python app.py starts the server on port 5000 with zero errors.
2. Navigating to http://127.0.0.1:5000 in a browser loads the upload form and file list.
3. Uploading any file (e.g., .txt, .jpg, .pdf) saves it inside file_share_app/shared_files/ and immediately displays its name in the webpage list.
4. Clicking a listed filename triggers a browser download of that exact file.
5. Navigating to http://<HOST-LOCAL-IP>:5000 from a second device on the same Wi-Fi network allows full upload and download functionality.

6. Rules & Constraints

• Allowed Libraries: Python Standard Library + Flask only.
• Prohibited: External databases (SQLite, PostgreSQL, etc.), JavaScript frameworks, or third-party cloud storage APIs.